<%# locals: subscription:

    The one word for what GitHub is doing with this hook right now. Extracted
    because two screens say it — /subscriptions and the watch control on a
    repository's own page — and a state whose wording differs between them is
    a state the reader has to work out twice. %>
<%# Order is deliberate. A stale callback outranks a suspension because a
    suspension heals itself on the next delivery and a stale callback means no
    delivery is arriving at all — so the suspension cannot heal until the
    address is fixed first. %>
<% if subscription.broken? %>
  <span class="pill-removed" data-testid="subscription-broken">Not working</span>
<% elsif subscription.callback_stale? %>
  <span class="pill-modified" data-testid="subscription-stale">Wrong address</span>
<% elsif subscription.suspended? %>
  <span class="pill-pending" data-testid="subscription-suspended">Retrying</span>
<% else %>
  <span class="pill-added">Active</span>
<% end %>
